      "value": "@{6472074f186643094cf0e11f|full_name}: I wonder if it's related to drivers. Make a note of the driver version you're using now, either GPU-Z or dxdiag can give you an exact version, and then depending on the exact version you might be able to get something newer, or try some sightly older drivers.\n\nWhen did you notice this? Hopefully it's just a driver related issue where information is being sightly mishandled, and not symptoms of a dying GPU (bad VRAM?)",
