      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I started experiencing these issues from the beginning of May until today. Prior to this, VRChat was not installed on my PC. I attempted to downgrade to the versions listed below. Surprisingly, after downgrading and then upgrading again to the original version, the issue was no longer reproducible. However, the problem did occur when I brought a different window to the foreground while VRChat was still visible. This isn't a big issue since it's not during gameplay, but these phenomena might provide some clues to understand what's going on. \n\nHere are the versions I've tried, in order from oldest to newest:\n\n- 465.89-desktop-win10-64bit-international-whql \n\n- 472.12-desktop-win10-win11-64bit-international-whql\n\n- 526.98-desktop-win10-win11-64bit-international-dch-whql\n\n- 528.24-desktop-win10-win11-64bit-international-dch-whql\n\n- 531.79-desktop-win10-win11-64bit-international-dch-whql\n\nThe current version is 31.0.15.3203 (NVIDIA). \n\nThank you for your assistance, Docteh.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
